        "additional_info": null,
        "result": {
          "type": "string",
          "value": "PASS"
        },
        "shell": "/usr/bin/osascript -l JavaScript -e 'var s = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.applicationaccess\"); (ObjC.unwrap(s.objectForKey(\"allowFingerprintForUnlock\")) == false && s.objectIsForcedForKey(\"allowFingerprintForUnlock\")) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"'"
      },
      "language": "bash"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "TouchID and OpticID enables the ability to unlock an Apple device with a user's fingerprint or iris.\n\nTouchID _MUST_ be disabled for \"Unlocking your Mac\" on all macOS devices that are capable of using Touch ID. OpticID _MUST_ be disabled for \"Unlocking your device\" on all devices that are capable of using OpticID.\n\nThe system _MUST_ remain locked until the user establishes access using an authorized identification and authentication method.\n\nNOTE: TouchID and OpticID is not an approved biometric authenticator for US Federal Government usage as it has not been verified to meet the strength requirements outlined in NIST SP 800-63.\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
